From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] airoha: ppe: evict stale flow_offload cookie on REPLACE + fix stale counter

flow_offload's FLOW_CLS_REPLACE may recycle a cookie that this driver
still has on record (when the core has not yet propagated its TEARDOWN
for the prior flow through the notifier chain). In that case
rhashtable_lookup() returns the existing entry, the old 999-91
returned -EEXIST, and the new SW arming silently failed -- F' never
got armed even though SWCOMMIT logs claimed success.

Fix: on REPLACE, if a stale entry exists for this cookie, evict it
(airoha_ppe_foe_flow_remove_entry + rhashtable_remove + kfree) BEFORE
adding the new one. DIAG REPLACE counter also fixed: previously
diag_replace_stale was incremented AFTER e was set to NULL in the
eviction block, so the counter was permanently 0 and the
stale-cookie-recycle signal was masked. Sample was_stale BEFORE
the eviction.

Signed-off-by: OpenWrt <noreply@openwrt.org>
---

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_ppe.c
@@ -1333,9 +1333,44 @@
 	int err, i, offload_type;
 	u16 addr_type = 0;
 
-	if (rhashtable_lookup(&eth->flow_table, &f->cookie,
-			      airoha_flow_table_params))
-		return -EEXIST;
+	e = rhashtable_lookup(&eth->flow_table, &f->cookie,
+			      airoha_flow_table_params);
+#ifdef CONFIG_NET_SWITCHDEV
+	/* DIAG (999-92): visibility on the FLOW_CLS_REPLACE path.
+	 * Throttle to 1/s; reports count of replace events in the
+	 * last 1 s window plus how many found a stale cookie.  A
+	 * non-zero stale count means the SW flow_offload core
+	 * recycled a cookie this driver still had on record.
+	 *
+	 * Note: was_stale is sampled BEFORE the eviction block below
+	 * sets e=NULL, otherwise the counter would always read 0 --
+	 * prior revisions had this bug and silently masked the
+	 * stale-cookie-recycle signal.
+	 */
+	{
+		static unsigned long diag_replace_last;
+		static u32 diag_replace_count, diag_replace_stale;
+		bool was_stale = (e != NULL);
+
+		diag_replace_count++;
+		if (was_stale)
+			diag_replace_stale++;
+		if (time_after(jiffies, diag_replace_last + HZ)) {
+			pr_info("DIAG REPLACE: %u/s stale=%u\n",
+				diag_replace_count, diag_replace_stale);
+			diag_replace_last = jiffies;
+			diag_replace_count = 0;
+			diag_replace_stale = 0;
+		}
+	}
+#endif
+	if (e) {
+		airoha_ppe_foe_flow_remove_entry(eth->ppe, e);
+		rhashtable_remove_fast(&eth->flow_table, &e->node,
+			       airoha_flow_table_params);
+		kfree(e);
+		e = NULL;
+	}
 
 	if (!flow_rule_match_key(rule, FLOW_DISSECTOR_KEY_META))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
